## Authentication

Every route under `/api/v1` needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; `/health`{{if .Observability}} and `/metrics`{{end}} stay public.
Tokens are HS256 JWTs with `sub` and `exp`, signed with `JWT_SECRET` by your identity service.
`go run ./cmd/token -sub alice` signs one for development. Handlers read the caller with
`auth.FromContext(ctx)`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Observability}}

## Metrics and tracing

`GET /metrics` serves `http_request_duration_seconds{method,route,status}` plus Go runtime metrics
for Prometheus. Every request gets an OpenTelemetry span that continues an incoming `traceparent`;
spans are exported when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set, and request logs carry `trace_id`
and `span_id`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}

## Cache

`{{.P.cache.Dir}}` stores JSON values in Redis with a TTL (`Get`, `Set`, `Delete`); keys are
prefixed with the service name. `/health` pings Redis too. Test against a real Redis with
`TEST_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/15 go test ./...`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Payment}}

## Payments

`{{.P.payment.Dir}}` builds the clients from the configuration; `cmd/server` creates them at start-up,
so pass them to the services that take payments. Start-up fails while a required variable is missing.
{{- if .QPay}}

- QPay (`github.com/techpartners-asia/qpay-go/qpay_v2`): `NewQPay` returns a client whose `Authorize(ctx)`
  logs in or refreshes the token; call it before each API call. After `qpay.ErrUnauthorized`, call
  `Reset` and `Authorize` and retry.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Bonum}}
- Bonum (`github.com/techpartners-asia/bonum-go`): `NewBonum` returns `*bonum.Client` (`Invoices`, `Cards`,
  `Subscriptions`, `QR`); it handles its own tokens. Verify webhooks with
  `bonum.ParseWebhook(body, header, cfg.Bonum.ChecksumKey)` on the raw body.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Golomt}}
- Golomt (`github.com/techpartners-asia/golomt-api-go`): `NewGolomt` returns the eCommerce and SocialPay
  clients; one is nil when its variables are not set.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
